# {{ project_name }} on Google Cloud Run

The generated Dockerfile uses the project root as its build context. From the
project root, copy it into place and deploy:

```sh
cp .pywire/deploy/gcp_cloudrun/Dockerfile ./Dockerfile
gcloud run deploy {{ project_name }} \
  --source . \
  --region us-central1
```

For WebSocket/session-affinity mode add `--session-affinity`; stateless mode does not need it.

## PYWIRE_SECRET_KEY

Stateless mode (`PyWire(stateless=True)`) signs client-held snapshots and needs
`PYWIRE_SECRET_KEY` in the service environment. Without it the container fails
to boot with `RuntimeError: PyWire(stateless=True) requires secret_key= or the
PYWIRE_SECRET_KEY env var`. Generate one at deploy time and pass it in the same
command (never commit it):

```sh
gcloud run deploy {{ project_name }} \
  --source . \
  --region us-central1 \
  --set-env-vars PYWIRE_SECRET_KEY="$(python -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))')"
```

For production prefer Secret Manager — store the value as a secret version,
then pass `--set-secrets PYWIRE_SECRET_KEY=NAME:latest` instead. Session-based
mode (no `stateless=True`) does not need the variable.
